#Windows Domains
## Objectives
Learn the purpose of a Windows Domain
## Key Components
| File Servers | central storage and sharepoint for files accessible to multiple users/computers |
| Database Servers | provides storage, organization and service of data for apps and app users |
| Workstations | client-user endpoint that runs client software and has limited access to domain services on the connected network |
| Desktops | domain connected device that runs the Windows GUI and provides interactive environment for end-users
## Security Relevance
- file servers should be monitored for excessive access/access at unusual times
- database servers handle critical information access should be limited to essential users
- workstations are common initial entry for malware due to contact with untrusted networks
## Key Takeaways
- domains enable efficient provisioning and security of the various components in a connnected network

